<title>HONG KONG: China Light year net down 14.8 pct.</title>
<headline>China Light year net down 14.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended September 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   242    vs 285</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    44     vs 37</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil    vs 1,286 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    4,836  vs 5,674</p>
<p>    Turnover		     18,620 vs 17,072</p>
<p>    Company name		 China Light and Power Co Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  November 27 to December 16</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   December 17</p>
<p>NOTE - China Light and Power is engaged in generation and supply of electricity in Hong Kong.</p>
<p>Comparative share earnings include the exceptional item. Excluding the exceptional item, the comparative share earnings were 220 H.K. cents.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 140 H.K. cents (including first interim dividend of 32 cents, second dividend of 32 cents and third dividend of 32 cents) vs 162 cents (including first interim dividend, second dividend, third dividend and special dividend).</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
